00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.440
I was six years old when I brought&nbsp;
my first cucumber to my mother.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:17.520
It was withered yellowing and approximately five&nbsp;
or six inches in length. But the immense pride I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.640
felt was unshaken. Watching the tendrils from the&nbsp;
cucumber plant curl around the trellis I provided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.840
for it was the first time I was consciously aware&nbsp;
of having a love of nature. Can you believe a 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.960
000-year-old traditional farming technology has&nbsp;
a place in today's high-tech greenhouses. My name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:38.320
is Jonah Helmer and I'm a sophomore at Cornell&nbsp;
University majoring in plant sciences with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:44.080
concentration in sustainability and a minor&nbsp;
in nutritional sciences. By the year 2050,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.800
we're going to need to double the world's food&nbsp;
supply in order to feed our growing population.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.920
My interest in sustainability has led me to&nbsp;
research aquaponics as a possible solution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:59.600
to this problem. I've worked in research projects&nbsp;
that assess the difference between hydroponic and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.800
aquaponic growing methods. I'm also the vice&nbsp;
president of the Cornell Hydroponics Club.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.880
I hope to use these experiences to&nbsp;
build a career growing sustainable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.600
nutritious, and affordable produce in&nbsp;
greenhouses accessible to urban populations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

